# EtCheckbox Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtCheckbox` is a controlled checkbox component for the eToro design system. It provides a flexible, accessible checkbox with:

- **Three variants**: square (default, supports indeterminate), round, and add (plus icon when unchecked)
- **Compound component pattern**: `EtCheckbox.Label` subcomponent
- **Built-in states**: checked, unchecked, error, indeterminate (square only)
- **Animated transitions**: smooth background, border, and icon animations
- **Haptic feedback**: enabled by default

**Does NOT handle:**

- Form validation logic (handle in parent)
- Checkbox group management (handle selection state in parent)
- Uncontrolled mode (always requires `value` + `onChange`)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtCheckbox` (main component)

```tsx
<EtCheckbox
  value: CheckboxValue          // required - controlled state
  onChange: (checked: boolean) => void  // required - toggle callback
  variant?: CheckboxVariant     // default: 'square'
  disabled?: boolean            // default: false
  haptics?: boolean             // default: true
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
>
  {children}
</EtCheckbox>
```

**Children constraints:**

- Optional: `EtCheckbox.Label` for text label
- String shorthand is NOT supported - use compound component

### `EtCheckbox.Label`

```tsx
<EtCheckbox.Label
  style?: StyleProp<TextStyle>
  disabled?: boolean            // auto-passed from parent
>
  {ReactNode}
</EtCheckbox.Label>
```

### Types

| Type                      | Values                                              |
| ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `CheckboxVariant`         | `'square'` \| `'round'` \| `'add'`                  |
| `CheckboxValueSquare`     | `true` \| `false` \| `'error'` \| `'indeterminate'` |
| `CheckboxValueRoundOrAdd` | `true` \| `false` \| `'error'`                      |

**Note:** TypeScript enforces correct value types per variant via discriminated union.

## Usage Patterns

### Basic (square variant)

```tsx
const [value, setValue] = useState<CheckboxValueSquare>(false);
<EtCheckbox value={value} onChange={setValue} />;
```

### With label

```tsx
<EtCheckbox value={value} onChange={setValue}>
  <EtCheckbox.Label>Subscribe to Newsletter</EtCheckbox.Label>
</EtCheckbox>
```

### Round variant

```tsx
const [value, setValue] = useState<CheckboxValueRoundOrAdd>(false);
<EtCheckbox value={value} onChange={setValue} variant="round" />;
```

### Add variant

```tsx
<EtCheckbox value={value} onChange={setValue} variant="add" />
```

### Indeterminate state (square only)

```tsx
<EtCheckbox value="indeterminate" onChange={setValue} variant="square" />
```

### Error state

```tsx
<EtCheckbox value="error" onChange={setValue} />
```

### Multi-selection pattern

```tsx
const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string[]>([]);

const toggleItem = (id: string, checked: boolean) => {
  setSelected((prev) => (checked ? [...prev, id] : prev.filter((item) => item !== id)));
};

{
  items.map((item) => (
    <EtCheckbox key={item.id} value={selected.includes(item.id)} onChange={(checked) => toggleItem(item.id, checked)}>
      <EtCheckbox.Label>{item.name}</EtCheckbox.Label>
    </EtCheckbox>
  ));
}
```

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Using string children (not supported)

```tsx
// BAD - EtCheckbox doesn't support string shorthand
<EtCheckbox value={value} onChange={setValue}>
  Subscribe
</EtCheckbox>
```

**Fix:** Always use compound component:

```tsx
<EtCheckbox value={value} onChange={setValue}>
  <EtCheckbox.Label>Subscribe</EtCheckbox.Label>
</EtCheckbox>
```

### ❌ Using indeterminate with round/add variants

```tsx
// BAD - TypeScript will error, indeterminate only valid for square
const [value, setValue] = useState<CheckboxValueRoundOrAdd>('indeterminate');
<EtCheckbox value={value} onChange={setValue} variant="round" />;
```

**Fix:** Use `CheckboxValueSquare` type only with `variant="square"`.

### ❌ Using wrong value type for variant

```tsx
// BAD - mixing value types
const [value, setValue] = useState<CheckboxValueSquare>(false);
<EtCheckbox value={value} onChange={setValue} variant="add" />;
```

**Fix:** Match value type to variant:

```tsx
// For square variant
const [value, setValue] = useState<CheckboxValueSquare>(false);

// For round or add variants
const [value, setValue] = useState<CheckboxValueRoundOrAdd>(false);
```

### ❌ Manually styling colors

```tsx
// BAD - bypasses design system
<EtCheckbox.Label style={{ color: 'red' }}>Label</EtCheckbox.Label>
```

**Fix:** Colors are automatically managed based on theme. Use `style` prop only for layout adjustments.

### ❌ Expecting toggled value in onChange

```tsx
// BAD - onChange always emits boolean (true or false)
<EtCheckbox
  value="indeterminate"
  onChange={(checked) => {
    // checked will be `true`, not the previous value
    setValue(checked ? 'indeterminate' : false); // Wrong!
  }}
/>
```

**Fix:** `onChange` emits the new checked state as boolean. Indeterminate/error → toggles to `true`, `true` → toggles to `false`.

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` - provides theme colors for styling
- `EtoroIcon` - underlying icon component (checkLine, plusLine)
- Hooks:
  - `useCheckboxConfig` - derives colors, size, borderRadius from props
  - `useCheckboxState` - manages animations and press handler
  - `useCheckboxChildren` - processes children with disabled prop

### External Dependencies

- `expo-haptics` - haptic feedback on press
- `react-native` - `Pressable`, `View`, `StyleSheet`
- `react-native-reanimated` - animations for background, border, scale, and icons

### Design System Integration

- Colors come from theme (`useEtoroTheme().colors`):
  - Checked: theme primary color
  - Unchecked: theme border color
  - Error: theme error color
  - Icon: white (inverted)
- Sizes:
  - Square: 24×24, 4px border radius
  - Round/Add: 30×30, fully round (15px radius)
- Icon size: 20px (fixed)

## Patterns & Pitfalls

### Controlled Component Pattern

The checkbox is always controlled - parent owns state via `value` + `onChange`:

- `value` determines visual state
- `onChange` receives toggled boolean (`true` or `false`)
- Never stores internal state

### onChange Behavior

`onChange` always emits a boolean, regardless of input state:

| Current Value     | onChange Emits |
| ----------------- | -------------- |
| `true`            | `false`        |
| `false`           | `true`         |
| `'error'`         | `true`         |
| `'indeterminate'` | `true`         |

### Variant Visual Differences

| Variant  | Unchecked    | Checked   |
| -------- | ------------ | --------- |
| `square` | Empty box    | Checkmark |
| `round`  | Empty circle | Checkmark |
| `add`    | Plus icon    | Checkmark |

### Indeterminate State

Only supported for `square` variant:

- Shows filled background (like checked)
- Does NOT show check icon
- Useful for "select all" with partial selection
- Clicking toggles to `true` (checked)

### Animation Behavior

Animations are handled by `useCheckboxState`:

- **Background**: Fades in/out with scale pulse (0.95 → 1)
- **Border**: Color transitions between unchecked/checked/error
- **Check icon**: Fades and scales in (0.3 → 1) at 70% of animation
- **Plus icon (add variant)**: Fades out and rotates when checking

Animation duration and easing are defined in `utils/animation-constants.ts`.

### Accessibility

Built-in accessibility support:

- `accessibilityRole="checkbox"`
- `accessibilityState={{ checked: isIndeterminate ? 'mixed' : isChecked }}`
- `accessibilityLabel` prop for custom screen reader text
- `hitSlop={{ top: 8, bottom: 8, left: 8, right: 8 }}` for easier touch

